# base/tiers/skolem -- SKOLEM INTRODUCTIONS. The only unit outside base/axioms
# that declares a bare axiom, and the list is enumerated in `base::SKOLEM`.
#
# §10's G1 table admits three forms. Two are definitional and carry zero
# content. The third is Skolem -- `exists! r. C(r)` together with
# `C(r) -> phi(r)` -- admissible when `exists r. phi(r)` is PROVED from earlier
# material, and conservative by model expansion rather than by definition.
#
# §10 says Skolem is needed "essentially just for Inf", and that is exactly
# right: FOUNDATION §11's correction to S3 records WHY. S3 justifies introducing
# a primitive by "conservative because |- exists x. phi(x)", but existence does
# not license UNIQUENESS -- Infinity's phi holds of MANY sets. So Inf cannot be
# given a definitional introduction the way Pow and Union are: it would satisfy
# EX and fail UNIQ, and a constant without UNIQ does not encode a function (S2).
#
# WHAT IS ADMITTED AND WHAT IS PROVED, kept apart deliberately:
#   Inf_intro  ADMITTED. Uniqueness by Skolemisation, not by proof.
#   Inf_prop   ADMITTED. Inf has the property Isabelle's axiom ascribes to it.
#   Inf_side_condition  PROVED, from axiom 15. This is the admissibility
#                       condition of §10's Skolem row -- without it the
#                       introduction would not be conservative, and it is
#                       discharged here rather than asserted.
#
# Isabelle's own `ZF_Base.infinity` is `0 : Inf & (ALL y:Inf. succ(y) : Inf)`,
# the `Inf(r) -> phi(r)` half. It is not statable in base/ because `succ` is a
# defined constant far down the definitional order, so phi is spelled
# relationally here -- the same statement, in the primitive signature.

axiom Inf_intro: exists r. (set(r) & (Inf(r) & (forall s. (Inf(s) -> eq(r,s)))))
axiom Inf_prop: forall r. (Inf(r) -> ((exists e. (set(e) & (elem(e,r) & (forall u. (set(u) -> (~ elem(u,e))))))) & (forall y. (set(y) -> (elem(y,r) -> (exists s. (set(s) & (elem(s,r) & (forall w. (set(w) -> (elem(w,s) <-> (elem(w,y) | eq(w,y)))))))))))))

claim Inf_side_condition: exists r. (set(r) & ((exists e. (set(e) & (elem(e,r) & (forall u. (set(u) -> (~ elem(u,e))))))) & (forall y. (set(y) -> (elem(y,r) -> (exists s. (set(s) & (elem(s,r) & (forall w. (set(w) -> (elem(w,s) <-> (elem(w,y) | eq(w,y)))))))))))))
claim Inf_EX: exists r. (set(r) & Inf(r))
claim Inf_UNIQ: forall r. (set(r) -> (forall s. (set(s) -> (Inf(r) -> (Inf(s) -> eq(r,s))))))
